      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14176224/assets/64fcf64e043698366083e24b6041e2fb406b725671ab71c0c871c7e708517685.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above. Which of the following statements is true?\n\nI. $∠A$ is a null angle\n\nII. $∠C$ is a full angle\n\nIII. $∠D$ is a right angle",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. From the diagram, $m∠A>{0}^{∘}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. From the diagram, $m∠C<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. From the diagram, $m∠D={90}^{∘}.$ Therefore, $∠D$ is a right angle.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
