    "q-52745": {
      "dom_id": "step-q52745",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Let $∠S$ and $∠T$ be two adjacent angles. Given that $∠S$ is a straight angle and $∠T$ is obtuse, what type of angle is their sum?",
      "worked_solution": "Since $∠S$ is a straight angle, we have \n\n$$\nm∠S={180}^{∘}.\n$$\n\n Since $∠T$ is obtuse, we have\n\n$$\n{90}^{∘}<m∠T<{180}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSo, the sum of these two angles satisfies by the following inequalies:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{180}^{∘}+{90}^{∘} & <m∠S+m∠T<{180}^{∘}+{180}^{∘} \\\\ {270}^{∘} & <m∠S+m∠T<{360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the sum of $∠S$ and $∠T$ is a reflex angle.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
