    "q-52647": {
      "dom_id": "step-q52647",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14176224/assets/a5752cefaad576ffeb18408db80dac554a525a0e4137b46377fee225436da433.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $∠AOB≅∠COD$ and $∠BOC≅∠DOE.$ Given that $m∠AOB=2m∠BOC$ and that $∠AOE$ is a straight angle, $m∠BOC=$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $∠AOB≅∠COD$ and $∠DOE≅∠BOC,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOB & =m∠COD \\\\ m∠BOC & =m∠DOE\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, since $∠AOE$ is a straight angle, we have $m∠AOE={180}^{∘}.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOB+m∠BOC+m∠COD+m∠DOE & =m∠AOE \\\\ m∠AOB+m∠BOC+m∠AOB+m∠BOC & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2m∠BOC+m∠BOC+2m∠BOC+m∠BOC & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 6m∠BOC & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠BOC & ={30}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
