    "q-171812": {
      "dom_id": "step-q171812",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14176224/assets/be311b9b624fba745b93d7ac3cd67ace3bbe4ea0650b12fa900d3aac50b5bae2.png)\n\nIn the figure shown above, the measure of $∠COF$ is{{field-1}}\n${}^{∘}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The angle addition postulate gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠EOD & =m∠EOB+m∠BOD \\\\  & ={82}^{∘}+{47}^{∘} \\\\  & ={129}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, $∠AOF$ and $∠EOD$ are vertical angles. Since vertical angles are congruent, we have \n\n$$\nm∠AOF=m∠EOD={129}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, since $∠AOC$ is a right angle, the angle addition postulate gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOF & =m∠AOC+m∠COF \\\\ {129}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘}+m∠COF \\\\ m∠COF & ={39}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
